# Genre -> channel mapping for create_movie_channels.py / create_mix_channels.py.
#
# One line per channel: "Channel Name: genre1, genre2, ..." — any Jellyfin
# Genres value not listed anywhere in this file is skipped (not
# auto-channeled), so start narrow and add lines as you go.
#
# Order matters: this file's line order IS the channel-numbering block
# order (see WORKFLOW.md), and it's the tie-breaker when a movie matches
# more than 2 genres (only the first 2 matches, in file order, are used).
# Don't reorder existing lines once you've created channels from them.
#
# Copy this file to channel_genres.txt and edit for your library's actual
# genre tags (check what Jellyfin reports with a quick browse of your
# library, or via Jellyfin's own API).

Action: Action
Sci-Fi: Science Fiction
Comedy: Comedy
Drama: Drama
Horror: Horror
Thriller: Thriller
Animation: Animation
